msgctxt "(dlgSgPreferences|dlgSgRepositorySettings).lbl:"
msgid "Enter regular expressions defining the grouping. Example: `refs\\\\/tags\\\\/build\\(?<name>.\\\\\\*\\)`"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "(dlgSgPreferences|dlgSgRepositorySettings).lbl:"
msgid "Optionally, enter regular expressions defining additional refs to preserve."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "(dlgSgPreferences|dlgSgRepositorySettings).ttpGroupPatterns:"
msgid "Example: <tt>build:refs/tags/build\\(?&lt;name&gt;.\\*\\),version:refs/tags/\\\\d+\\\\.\\\\d+\\\\..\\*</tt>"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "(dlgSgPreferences|dlgSgRepositorySettings).ttpGroupPatterns:"
msgid "Next, the refs remaining in the group will be passed on from child to parent commit. Now, once again they will be assigned to matching groups, possibly replacing other refs or possibly becoming replaced by more recent refs."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "(dlgSgPreferences|dlgSgRepositorySettings).ttpGroupPatterns:"
msgid "Patterns will be matched against the full ref-name, including the <tt>refs</tt>-prefix. For a matching ref, its name will be shortened to the last path-segment \\('\\\\/'\\). For example, <tt>refs/tags/build-.\\*</tt> will match a tag <tt>refs/tags/build-123</tt> and its name will be shortened to <tt>build-123</tt>. You may add a <i>named regex capturing group</i> called <tt>name</tt> to further customize the name extraction. For example, <tt>refs/tags/build-\\(?&lt;name&gt;.\\*\\)</tt> will match <tt>refs/tags/build-123</tt> and its name will be shortened to <tt>123</tt>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "(dlgSgPreferences|dlgSgRepositorySettings).ttpGroupPatterns:"
msgid "Refs will be categorized into groups: when traversing the repository root log, refs will first be assigned to matching groups. Every group will store only the most recently encountered ref, i.e. if a new ref is encountered, it will replace all existing refs in the current group."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "(dlgSgPreferences|dlgSgRepositorySettings).ttpGroupPatterns:"
msgid "You can assign a title to a pattern by prefixing it by <tt>title:</tt>; the title may only contain letters, digits and '_'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "(dlgSgPreferences|dlgSgRepositorySettings).ttpGroupPatterns:"
msgid "You can specify multiple groups patterns, separated by comma \\(<tt>,</tt>\\), which will be processed in the specified order: if you define two groups which both match a set of refs, such refs will be assigned to the first group."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "(dlgSgPreferences|dlgSgRepositorySettings).ttpSinglePattern:"
msgid "Example: <tt>refs\\\\/remotes\\\\/origin\\\\/release-.\\\\\\*</tt>"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "(dlgSgPreferences|dlgSgRepositorySettings).ttpSinglePattern:"
msgid "For example, you want to make sure that each of your release branches is considered as group on its own and thus show up in the log graph or will be treated separately by the 'on-refs' calculation."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "(dlgSgPreferences|dlgSgRepositorySettings).ttpSinglePattern:"
msgid "In addition to the grouping logic, a ref matching the <b>Single Patterns</b> will be assigned to a group on its own. This is a shortcut for enumerating each of these refs as explicit pattern in <b>Group Patterns</b>."
msgstr ""

